Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Mr. Chair, point of order.

asr-000593
00:24:56.370 --> 00:25:00.410
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Well, considering there was a motion which was properly seconded,

asr-000594
00:25:01.410 --> 00:25:04.750
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: the proper course of action would be to divide the house.

asr-000595
00:25:05.050 --> 00:25:15.790
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: But if our good friend, Congress Mantino, would limit the questions to the budget submitted,

asr-000596
00:25:15.990 --> 00:25:21.730
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: then I will not insist that we divide the house and proceed with the motion.

asr-000597
00:25:21.730 --> 00:25:26.050
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Since we did not divide the house and I asked for permission from the source person,

asr-000598
00:25:26.050 --> 00:25:30.370
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: whether they are willing to answer a few questions,

asr-000599
00:25:30.890 --> 00:25:33.750
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: maybe we will hold the motion in abeyance.

asr-000600
00:25:34.530 --> 00:25:37.090
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pagkatapos, we take it up after the few questions.

asr-000601
00:25:37.450 --> 00:25:38.010
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung pwede lang.

asr-000602
00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:42.030
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: We'll just ask Congressman Nassal to withhold the motion first.

asr-000603
00:25:42.830 --> 00:25:47.470
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Congressman Nassal, can you make your motion static in nature for a while

asr-000604
00:25:47.470 --> 00:25:52.110
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: so that we can allow the minority to ask questions to the resource person?

asr-000605
